      "message": "**File:** `util/egis/egis_util.h` \u0026 `util/egis/et171_flash.cc`\n\nWhile your usage of `std::ranges::find` invoking the `(iterator, iterator)` constructor of `std::string_view` is valid C++20/23, doing it inline is verbose. Google Style strongly encourages writing small, readable helper functions for text manipulation.\n\nAdd this C++23 compliant helper to `egis_util.h`:\n\n```c\n// Safely creates a string_view from a fixed-size character array that may\n// or may not be null-terminated.\ntemplate \u003csize_t N\u003e\nconstexpr std::string_view MakeStringView(const char (\u0026str)[N]) {\n  auto end_it \u003d std::ranges::find(str, \u0027\\0\u0027);\n  return std::string_view(str, end_it);\n}\n\n```\n\nThen, update your print statements in `et171_flash.cc` for a massive readability win:\n\n```c\n  std::println(\"\\n--- Parsed Version Info ---\");\n  std::println(\"RO Version: {}\", MakeStringView(response.ro_ver));\n  std::println(\"RW Version: {}\", MakeStringView(response.rw_ver));\n\n```\n\nAlso update the usage in `PrintDeviceDiagnostics`.",
